## 2. Task Tables

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1: Compute Order of Storage Visits** | Robot computes the optimal order of storage visits based on waiting time and path. | AND | Robot’s onboard computer | 1 | The computation is performed by the robot’s internal system. |
| **AT2: Send Request Message to Storage** | Robot sends a request message to the storage with the precise specification of requested resources. | AND | Storage location | 1 | Direct interaction with the storage system. |
| **AT3: Wait for Resource Retrieval** | Robot waits until the storage retrieves the requested resources. | AND | Storage location | 1 | The robot remains at the storage until the resources are ready. |
| **AT4: Continue Collection** | Robot continues to the next storage location to collect resources. | OR | Next storage location | 1 | Executed when battery is sufficient. |
| **AT5: Go to Recharge Station & Assign Mission** | Robot goes to the recharge station and assigns the remaining mission to another robot. | OR | Recharge station | 1 | Executed when battery < 10 %. |
| **AT6: Transport Resources to Destination** | Robot transports the collected resources to the destination location. | AND | Destination location | 1 | Concrete delivery action. |
| **AT7: Return Resource to Checkpoint & Assign Remaining Task** | Robot returns the resource to a checkpoint and assigns remaining delivery task to another robot. | OR | Checkpoint | 1 | Executed when battery < 30 %. |
| **AT8: Continue Delivery** | Robot continues delivery of resources to destination. | OR | Destination location | 1 | Executed when battery is sufficient. |
| **AT9: Send Alert to Sector Manager** | Robot triggers an alert and reports failure to sector manager. | AND | Sector manager | 1 | Failure reporting action. |
| **AT10: Assign Multiple Robots to Parallel Collect‑Deliver Tasks** | Command center assigns multiple robots to parallel collect‑deliver tasks. | AND | Command center | 1 | Coordination action. |
| **AT11: Execute Parallel Collect‑Deliver Tasks** | Multiple robots execute parallel collect‑deliver tasks across different storages and destinations. | AND | Multiple storages/destinations | [2,5] | Range to accommodate variable number of robots. |

